// Title: Type::diff walks two tuple types that share their parts as trees
//        (setops::held_by_shape keeps no answer of a pair of nodes), so the
//        check of a two-arm select doubles with each level of nesting.
// Command: time timeout -s KILL 120 /home/eric/tmp/review-2026-11-16/bin/graphix --no-cache --check \
//          design/review-2026-11-16/repro/t-setops-held-by-shape-dag.gx
// Expected: about 0.1 s, as without the last line (the 54 lets alone, or
//           the two chains under `A(..) and `B(..)).
// Observed (debug binary): 22 s at this depth, 26; 5.6 s at 24, 1.5 s at
//           22, 0.43 s at 20, 0.18 s at 18: twice the time per level.
